  "summary": "I am an engineer with 4 years of industry experience writing and debugging code. Most of my work experience has been with C and C++, although I also write Python and bash scripts whenever possible to make repetitive tasks more efficient. In addition, I have some academic experience with Java, Android Studio, and training neural networks with TensorFlow in Python, as well as a bit of Verilog and assembly. I'm also a huge fan of developing on Linux thanks to its powerful command line and the greatest text editor ever invented, vim. \n\nI love developing software because it's so conducive to entering a flow state in which I find myself completely immersed and focused on the task at hand. Solving problems has always been fun to me, and the almost addicting sense of gratification that comes after struggling with one is present in coding more than any other endeavor that I have yet to experience. \n\nI'm thankful to have a career in such an exciting industry, and can't wait to see what the future brings.",
